  <sharedSelectionEntries>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Expendable" hidden="false" id="51b6-cea6-aa88-c8e5">
      <rules>
        <rule name="Expendable" id="88ad-a94e-6ff0-ba20" hidden="false">
          <description>The opposing player never gains Victory points for removing a unit that includes any models with this special rule as casualties. However, if a unit that includes any models with this special rule fails a Morale check, it does not Fall Back, but instead all models in the unit are removed from play as casualties immediately.

Armies of Dark Compliance: a unit given Expendable loses the Line Sub-type.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
      </costs>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Army of Dark Compliance" hidden="false" id="12cc-71f9-31de-349a">
      <rules>
        <rule name="Army of Dark Compliance" id="6e4b-96ab-9b89-4676" hidden="false">
          <description>An Army of Dark Compliance Detachment is a Primary Detachment using the Crusade Force Organisation Chart, built from both the Legiones Astartes and Imperialis Militia army lists.

Effects
• All its units count as the same Faction for all Core and Special Rules, including wargear, transports and special rules.
• It may not take Legiones Astartes Rites of War, but an Imperialis Militia Force Commander may take Provenances of War as normal.
• Any unit with the Militia Sub-type and without Independent Character may be given Expendable; a unit with Expendable loses the Line Sub-type.
• All models with Legiones Astartes (X) gain The Warmaster's Due.

Limitations
• It may only be a Primary Detachment in an army using the Crusade Force Organisation Chart, and the army must be Traitor.
• All its Legiones Astartes units must share the same Legiones Astartes (X) variant, and the army may not include an Allied Detachment of that Faction. Otherwise it counts as the Imperialis Militia Sub-faction of the Imperial Army for the Allies Matrix.
• It may not take a Primarch, and the Warlord must be a model with Legiones Astartes (X).
• It may never have more units with Legiones Astartes (X) than units with the Militia or Third-Line Sub-types.
• Models with Legiones Hereticus (X) may not be taken.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="The Warmaster's Due" id="ad26-13ce-cbc6-0007" hidden="false" targetId="640a-b320-41c3-0571" type="rule"/>
      </infoLinks>
